@* TotpLoginPage: the second step of signing in with a second factor, at "/login/totp".

   Static server-side rendered like the sign-in page: an ordinary HTML form that posts to /auth/login-totp (with an
   antiforgery token), so the endpoint can set the sign-in cookie. The page is reached after the user name and password
   were accepted; who is signing in is remembered by the server and a cookie of the browser, so the page shows no
   user name and has no user name field. Without a valid pending sign-in (none, expired, or from another address)
   the page sends the user back to the sign-in page with "error=totp-expired". A wrong code comes back here with
   "error=1"; the message is the same whatever went wrong. A client that made too many attempts comes back with
   "error=throttled". *@
@page "/login/totp"

<PageTitle>Second step - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<main class="page narrow" data-testid="totp-login-page">
    <h1>Enter your code</h1>

    <section class="card">
        <form method="post" action="/auth/login-totp" data-testid="totp-login-form">
            <AntiforgeryToken />
            <div class="field">
                <label for="totp-login-code">Code</label>
                <input id="totp-login-code" name="code" type="text" inputmode="text" maxlength="24"
                       autocomplete="one-time-code" autocapitalize="characters" spellcheck="false"
                       data-testid="totp-code-input" />
                <p class="muted hint">The 6-digit code from your authenticator app, or one of your recovery codes.</p>
            </div>
            @if (Throttled)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="totp-login-throttled">Too many attempts. Try again in a few minutes.</p>
            }
            else if (Failed)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="totp-login-error">That code is not valid, or it was already used.</p>
            }
            <button type="submit" data-testid="totp-login-button">Sign in</button>
        </form>
        <p><a href="/login" data-testid="totp-login-cancel">Back to sign in</a></p>
    </section>
</main>
